{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe light here in Vienna is peculiar, softening the edges of things. I spent the afternoon at the Belvedere; the paintings do not shout, but they hold a quiet dignity that speaks to the mind without demanding it.\n\nTonight, however, the mind was overwhelmed by the senses. I attended Rossini’s *Barber of Seville*. The Partheys, as I urged them, were there to share the experience. Lablache’s Figaro is a marvel of wit, and the company’s energy is infectious. The audience’s applause was not merely polite; it was a collective affirmation of the joy on stage, breaking the usual reserve of the Viennese. It reminded me that art, at its height, is the liberation of spirit through form.\n\nI am tired but happy. The journey is long, but such moments make the miles worthwhile. Think of me as I sit here, writing by candlelight, longing for our table in Berlin.\n\nYour loving,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080393,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":211,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1163,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-w9d6uLBUannrWAYy5SOWRHxxIXwBVzSE","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":957.517,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.005795168067227,"prompt_per_second":994.2382224023177,"predicted_n":211,"predicted_ms":5000.163,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.810299999999998,"predicted_per_second":41.99863084463447}}